  "_design": {
    "notes": "Burst-scroll-pause-reverse, the shape of an actual stack read. 30 fps is the burst rate inside a run, not a sustained demand: dwells are ~44% of the trace. Four direction reversals put stale frames in flight ahead of the wanted one, which is the only condition under which head-of-line blocking on a shared stream can cost anything."
  }
